    Act 19 §3: single-source per-office failure-event recorder + supervisor
    decision point (issue #4Ux4sxiHjpXqSi9T9d2suq-alabama)
    
    A terminal appointment (failed/stopped/killed) no longer causes an immediate
    new disposable Antonina ID or a registry overwrite.
    
    Recorder (single source): liveness/failures/events.tsv is the per-office
    failure-event ledger; every office supervisor (branch-bootstrap,
    terminal-continuity, seat-liveness, clerk-liveness, sitting) records every
    terminal appointment event into it. The row is extended: terminal_state
    (failed|stopped|killed), transient_flag, retry_safe (from
    backend_error.automatic_retry_safe/transient) and a durable evidence_path
    captured via terminal-appointment-evidence.sh once per agent
    (oc_capture_terminal_evidence). Legacy rows stay readable.
    
    Supervisor decision point: oc_supervisor_replacement_due (office-
    continuity.sh) is consulted before any replacement (branch-bootstrap,
    terminal-continuity, sitting; clerk/seat liveness go through terminal-
    continuity, which consults it). Replacement is due when either
      (1) the Act 19 §3.1 threshold reset is due (oc_reset_due: three distinct
          transient failures inside the window, progress guard, cooldown); or
      (2) terminal-continuity is due: a terminal state is recorded, the newest
          ledger terminal event has aged past oc_cooldown, and no reset has
          been recorded since that event.
    A terminal appointment by itself never replaces: terminal-continuity defers
    (exit 1, no replacement) while the decision point is not due; sitting
    triggers the shared terminal-continuity path when due and re-resolves the
    seat; branch-bootstrap no longer exits 1 when terminal continuity defers.
    
    Tests:
    - New real-integration test:
      tests/office-failure-recorder-integration-smoke.sh (real appointments.sh,
      branch-bootstrap.sh, terminal-continuity.sh, sitting.sh + mock Antonina):
      single terminal failures do not replace; the decision point is not-due
      while events are fresh; the Act 19 threshold replaces once; the aged
      terminal-continuity boundary replaces; sitting consults the decision
      point and replaces at threshold through it.
    - tests/terminal-continuity-o1-smoke.sh: control updated to the
      no-immediate-replacement semantics (fresh terminal event → deferred, no
      replacement; aged event → replacement).
    - tests/institutional-recovery-smoke.sh: same control update (terminal 5xx
      recorded in the ledger; deferred while fresh; replacement when aged).
    - act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh and clerk-liveness-smoke.sh already
      delegate to the real integration path (appointment-recovery-integration
      smoke); the new real test covers the recorder/decision point there.
    
    Full suite: sh tests/run-all.sh → All Viche tests passed.

